Root cause:
The bug was caused by not properly managing the runtime power management (PM) state during error handling in the `vpif_probe` function. Specifically, if an error occurred after enabling runtime PM but before the function completed successfully, the runtime PM would remain enabled, leading to an unbalanced state. The patch ensures that runtime PM is disabled before returning on probe errors, thus maintaining proper resource management and preventing potential issues related to power management.
